course: dictionary
lesson: 1317
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Cake usually means a sweet baked food, like the home-made cake in «Sometimes an action, like a home-made cake, says sorry better than words.» Here the cake is a gift, and the sentence tells you it is a way of saying sorry.
explain: A cake can also be a flat, round piece of other food, such as a fish cake. Context tells you which meaning to use: a fish cake is not sweet, and nobody bakes it in a tin for a birthday party.
explain: Cake can even be a verb. To be caked in mud is to be thickly covered in it. Read the words around the word, try each meaning in the sentence, and pick the one that makes sense.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Cake» usually means a sweet baked food, made from flour, eggs, sugar and butter.
fact: A cake can also be a flat, round piece of other food, such as a fish cake.
fact: «Caked» means thickly covered, as in caked in mud.
fact: «A piece of cake» is an idiom meaning something very easy.
exercise: «Sometimes an action, like a home-made cake, says sorry better than words.» What is a home-made cake here? | *A sweet baked food made at home | A cake of soap for washing | A flat stone on the beach | A fish cake from the shop
exercise: Ella's dinner is a fish cake. Which meaning of cake is this? | *A flat, round piece of other food | A sweet baked food for a party | To be thickly covered in mud | A small dried grape
exercise: Tom's boots were caked in mud. What does caked mean here? | *Thickly covered | Very clean and shiny | Cut into equal pieces | Sweet and sticky
test: Maths is «a piece of cake» for Ella, and she finished it in a minute. What does «a piece of cake» mean? | Cut into equal pieces | Made of sugar | *Very easy | Dropped on the floor
test: If you cut a cake into four equal pieces, what is each piece? | A half of the cake | A cupcake | *A quarter of the cake | A whole cake
exam: How can you find out which meaning of cake is right in a sentence? | Skip it and never read that sentence again | *Read the words around it and check which meaning fits | Look only at the first letter of the word | Guess the first meaning you think of
